{
  /* Build config — `tsc -b tsconfig.build.json` emits dist/, and this is the
     project the root, app, and planner-ui tsconfigs reference. The test
     exclude belongs here rather than in tsconfig.json (see the note there)
     so co-located *.test.ts files never ship in dist. */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": true,
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./tsconfig.build.tsbuildinfo",
    "noEmit": false,
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "dist",
    "declaration": true,
    "stripInternal": true
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  /* symbolLines.ts imports the typescript devDependency; it serves the
     conformance/freshness suites and the coverage publisher
     (rules-coverage.mjs, via rule-tooling-shared.mjs) only, so it stays out
     of dist like the tests do.

     The four rules/ modules after it are excluded for the same reason, and
     none is reachable through the exports map: `./rules` publishes only the
     taxRuleRegistry barrel, and there is no `./rules/*` wildcard.
     - describeRule.ts and its outOfScope sibling describeRefusal.ts import
       `vitest`, so a consumer who did reach either would fault on a bare
       framework import in a package the README promises is framework-free.
       Every importer is a `*.test.ts`.
     - coverageAttestations.ts and its per-directory shards under
       src/rules/attestations/ (formerly one ~116 KB file, now composed from
       the shards the same way taxRuleRegistry.ts composes records/*.ts) and
       coverageReport.ts are the coverage publisher's inputs, read from
       source by the tests and by rules-coverage.mjs, never from dist.
     Together they were ~146 KB of test-harness code in every install. */
  "exclude": [
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test-support.ts",
    "src/rules/symbolLines.ts",
    "src/rules/describeRefusal.ts",
    "src/rules/describeRule.ts",
    "src/rules/coverageAttestations.ts",
    "src/rules/attestations/**",
    "src/rules/coverageReport.ts"
  ]
}
